   "html_text": "The trouble then is that claims that people do have a capacity for a priori knowledge seem quite precarious. As we noted earlier (footnote 7), people are often unreliable at appreciating deductively valid arguments; and appreciating the standard rules even of natural deduction is for many people often a difficult intellectual achievement. Consequently, people’s general competence with logical notions may not in fact consist in any grip on valid logical rules; and so whatever rules do underlie th",
